---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const breadcrumbItems = [
  { name: 'Editorial Standards & Fact-Checking' }
];

const lastUpdated = "September 1, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Standards & Policy | Atrium Livings"
  description="Discover Atrium Livings's editorial governance, primary source verification protocols, AI transparency standards, and correction policies."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbItems}
  noindex={true}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbItems} />

  <div class="legal-page-container">
    <div class="container legal-content-wrapper">
      <header class="legal-header">
        <span class="legal-kicker">E-E-A-T Editorial Charter</span>
        <h1 class="legal-title">Editorial Policy & Fact-Checking Standards</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">Effective Date: {lastUpdated} &bull; Atrium Livings Media Group, Inc.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal-prose">
        <p class="lead">Atrium Livings adheres to the highest journalistic ethics and Google Search Essentials principles regarding Experience, Expertise, Authoritativeness, and Trustworthiness (E-E-A-T). This charter outlines our protocols for verification, author credentials, AI utilization, and corrections.</p>

        <h2>1. Author Qualifications & Editorial Oversight</h2>
        <p>Every article published on Atrium Livings is conceived, written, or curated by experienced creators. Our editorial team includes interior decorators, DIY makers, furniture specialists, and passionate home styling writers.</p>
        <p>Before any decorating tutorial, DIY guide, or room makeover advice is published, it undergoes editorial review to ensure practical clarity, safety, and actionable instructions for everyday homeowners.</p>

        <h2>2. Fact-Checking & Primary Sourcing</h2>
        <p>We mandate accurate, real-world verification for all practical advice:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Home Safety & DIY Best Practices:</strong> We follow established manufacturer safety guidelines, standard residential dimensions, and electrical/fire safety practices for all home projects.</li>
          <li><strong>Material Specifications:</strong> We verify product finishes, paint types, fabric durability, and lumber standards directly with reputable suppliers and experienced makers.</li>
          <li><strong>Renovation Budgets:</strong> Cost data is gathered from realistic project invoices, actual DIY material costs, and real homeowner budgets—not inflated or outdated estimates.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Artificial Intelligence (AI) Policy & Transparency</h2>
        <p>Atrium Livings is an original, human-driven home decor and DIY magazine. We do NOT publish automated, bulk AI-generated articles. While our researchers may utilize machine learning tools for statistical indexing or grammar consistency, all editorial prose, design ideas, styling tips, and DIY tutorials are created and verified by human specialists.</p>

        <h2>4. Corrections & Updates Protocol</h2>
        <p>We are committed to swift transparency whenever errors occur. If a factual, typographical, or technical error is identified in an article:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>We update the copy immediately with corrected information.</li>
          <li>We append a dated "Correction Note" at the conclusion of the article explaining the modification.</li>
          <li>Readers and industry professionals can submit fact-checking alerts directly to our ombudsman at <a href="mailto:intouchmagazines26@gmail.com">intouchmagazines26@gmail.com</a>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Commercial Conflicts of Interest</h2>
        <p>Our writers, photographers, and editors are strictly forbidden from accepting financial kickbacks, gifts exceeding nominal value ($25), or equity stakes in brands covered in our editorial columns. Advertisers and sponsors have zero oversight or advance approval rights over editorial content.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page-container {
    padding: 4rem 0 6rem;
  }
  .legal-content-wrapper {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .legal-header {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .legal-kicker {
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 2.75rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .legal-meta {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-text-light);
  }
  .legal-prose {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #2D2A26;
  }
  .legal-prose .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--color-text-main);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .legal-prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-main);
  }
  .legal-prose p {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  .legal-prose ul {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }
  .legal-prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-prose a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>